Summary:
During today’s session, we focused on structuring and integrating the frontend and backend components of the Developer Portfolio Evaluator project. We organized the project into proper folders and connected the React interface with the Node.js backend API. Several issues were encountered during execution, including module errors, API connection failures, and request handling problems, which were systematically debugged. We refined the controller logic, ensured correct API calls to GitHub, and verified data flow between client and server. The application was tested with real GitHub usernames to confirm proper functionality.

Outcomes:
By the end of the session, the application was successfully running with seamless communication between frontend and backend. The system was able to fetch real-time GitHub data and generate accurate repository counts and scores. Errors related to dependency installation, API requests, and server connectivity were resolved effectively. We also validated the correctness of results by comparing API responses with actual GitHub profiles. This improved understanding of full-stack integration, debugging practices, and real-world API handling.
